      "writtenOn": "2020-08-14T22:08:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking about the case the CL mentioned, i.e.\n1) Call mutex_lock before task switching\n2) Task switching started\n3) Call mutex_unlock\n\nUsually, the mutex_lock and mutex_unlock are paired to protect a small piece of code. In this above case, the mutex_look may be in some HOOK_INIT call, and the mutex_unlock has to be in some task context. This open end usage is problematic and considered to be a bad practice.",
